    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0560" n="436" xml:id="pg436"/>

                <head>No. 260.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morton to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 15,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Hare had no interview with the President since the two reported in my dispatch
                    No. 58. Can recall nothing to add to that reported except that at my second
                    visit the President corrected a statement of Mr. Rosas, who had understood him
                    to say that in my first visit I had declared my government did not desire
                    European assistance. This brought the explicit declaration reported in my
                    dispatch. Indications here apparently less favorable for recognition.</p>
                <closer><signed>MORTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
